  "id": "COMPOUND:20458 - PROTEIN:4972",
  "verbalization": "Lanostane is implicated in the target pathway leading to LAMA-84 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Lanostane acts as a target for multiple compounds, with MIP being a common intermediate in these relationships. MIP is identified as the target of both Lanostane and another compound, Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, which in turn targets LAMA-84. This indicates a potential shared mechanism of action or a common pathway in which Lanostane and its related compounds interact with LAMA-84. The presence of a complex, multi-step target pathway involving a structurally diverse set of compounds supports the idea that Lanostane may exert its effects through a broad, non-specific mechanism, possibly involving a common target or a shared biochemical pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Lanostane and LAMA-84, emphasizing the role of MIP as a central node in this network.",
